WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:03.436
[tense music]

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:08.341
CHRISTIAN: You'll never get the
truth from a current extremist.

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:11.978
Their whole job is to
lie to you and to spin

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.147
things their own way.

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:15.915
Which is why I say,
if you want the truth,

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:18.051
talk to a former extremist.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:19.519
JOURNALIST: You still
have the jacket?

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.021
CHRISTIAN: I still
have the jacket.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.223
JOURNALIST: Oh.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.824
CHRISTIAN: So this
was CASH, Chicago

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:28.795
Area Skinheads, which was that
first American neo-Nazi group.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:29.796
And then on the back--

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.166
JOURNALIST: Final Solution, wow.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.868
Final Solution
was my band name

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:38.004
with the 88, which
is kind of shorthand

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.973
for the eighth letter
of the alphabet, HH,

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:41.441
which stands for "Heil Hitler."

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.009
What was the final solution?

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.711
CHRISTIAN: Well, the
final solution in my mind

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:47.914
was the same thing that
was in Hitler's mind,

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:50.016
and that was the
extermination of the Jews.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.685
That was the ultimate solution.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.288
JOURNALIST (VOICEOVER):
From the age of 14 to 22,

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.756
Christian Vittrilini
helped build

00:00:56.823 --> 00:01:00.460
America's first neo-Nazi
skinhead organization.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.595
But today, he has
devoted his life

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.765
to helping people disengage
from the same extremist

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.167
groups he used to belong to.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.469
CHRISTIAN: What I see when
I look at those pictures

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.837
is not a tough guy.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:16.509
I see a very insecure,
low self-esteem,

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.545
and broken young man.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.480
And I think it's
important for people

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:23.550
to understand that what draws
people to those movements,

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.052
hate movements, is not
the ideology initially.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.320
Nobody is born to hate.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.988
It's something that we learn.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.925
And for me, I was
searching for an identity,

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.893
a community, and a purpose.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.195
JOURNALIST
(VOICEOVER): Christian

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.764
was ripe for radicalization.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:40.400
And on a street
corner in 1987, he

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.802
was approached by
a skinhead leader

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.505
and recruited on the spot.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.974
CHRISTIAN: That man
told me that I mattered.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.709
Nobody had ever
told me that before.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:53.112
And I bought into the ideas
that they put in my head

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.348
because it made
me feel powerful.

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:58.451
INTERVIEWER: With me today,
Chris Vittrilini, 19-years-old,

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:00.787
director of the Illinois
chapter of the Northern

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:01.921
Hammer Skinheads.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.523
Well, I believe
we're warriors today

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.125
and we're fighting for a great
cause, which is the white race.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.127
CHRISTIAN: I noticed my
life change immediately.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.330
I went from somebody
who had been bullied

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.764
to now somebody who was feared.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.066
JOURNALIST
(VOICEOVER): Christian

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.301
describes his
radicalization as a descent

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:18.404
into a community of
like-minded individuals.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:22.375
They consumed a potent mix of
race-based conspiracy theories

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:25.945
and misinformation
that fueled their anger

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:28.348
and justified their attacks.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:32.619
I wonder how that radicalization
process compares to today.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.221
(SINGING) Damn [inaudible]
just call me a shrink.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.323
CHRISTIAN: In my day, it
was very face to face.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:40.493
But what's happened
now is the internet

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.429
has kind of become that
digital alley that I was

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.832
recruited in, except
it's an all you can eat,

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:48.067
24 hour, hate buffet.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:51.204
And there are millions and
millions of young people

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.839
like I was at 14-years-old.

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.474
What about the
El Paso shooter?

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:57.210
CHRISTIAN: The whole idea of
a lone wolf is a misnomer.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.711
While there are white
supremacists who

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:01.981
may never in real life meet
another white supremacist,

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.284
that doesn't mean
they're not connected.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.885
JOURNALIST (VOICEOVER):
The internet

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:10.089
is a technological game changer,
amplifying lies and weaponizing

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:12.659
propaganda like never before.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:15.795
Extremists are flooding social
media and encrypted chat

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:21.134
forums, creating an alternate
universe of imaginary threats

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:26.539
where lies become truth and
conspiracy becomes reality.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:32.145
As of May 2021, Facebook
banned 250 groups

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:34.681
linked to white supremacy.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:38.318
Often what starts as edgy
memes that target young men

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:42.021
on platforms like Reddit,
Twitter, and others, quickly

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:45.158
spirals into more
extreme content.

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:47.393
The El Paso shooter,
for example,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.997
wrote that he was inspired
by a manifesto posted online

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:54.100
by a shooter in New
Zealand who livestreamed

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:57.437
himself murdering 51 Muslims.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:01.007
Called "The Great Replacement,"
this manifesto justified

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:03.943
the killings as a
defense of white culture

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.813
from the existential
threat posed by Muslims,

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.215
minorities, and immigrants.

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:11.884
The fact that these
white genocide fears have

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:15.121
been debunked time and
again over centuries

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:17.223
means little online.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.559
Within the echo chamber
of the movement,

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:23.663
the New Zealand shooter's
manifesto is revered and used

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:26.199
to indoctrinate new recruits.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:28.868
All too often,
that's how it works.

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:31.504
The speed of online
radicalisation

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:35.742
helps explain why race-based
attacks are on the rise.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:41.481
As Christian said, nobody is
born to hate, it's learned.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:45.018
[upbeat music]

